<h2>Journey 1: a developer's first day with the Cloud edition</h2>
<ol class="steps-list">
  <li><strong>Opens the link</strong> a colleague shared. Sees the landing page with "Sign in with Atlassian" and "Try with sample data".</li>
  <li><strong>Signs in</strong>. Atlassian asks which Jira site to share and shows the read-only permissions. They click Accept. (<a href="flow-signin.html">What happens underneath</a>.)</li>
  <li><strong>Lands on For You</strong>, greeted by name, seeing every bug assigned to them.</li>
  <li><strong>Opens JARVIS</strong>, clicks <em>Enable</em> for background notifications, allows the browser prompt, presses <em>Test announcement</em> and hears the voice.</li>
  <li><strong>Closes the laptop.</strong> Within minutes of a colleague reopening one of their bugs, their phone or desktop shows "ABC-123 was reopened". (<a href="flow-push.html">The notification's journey</a>.)</li>
  <li><strong>Next morning</strong> they open the dashboard; JARVIS says "Good morning. While you were away, 3 things happened across 2 of your bugs."</li>
</ol>

<h2>Journey 2: a lead reviewing an epic</h2>
<ol class="steps-list">
  <li>Switches to <strong>Epics</strong>, pastes the epic's Jira URL into the Track box.</li>
  <li>Reads the progress bar and KPIs: 34 open, 9 older than 7 days, 4 unassigned.</li>
  <li>Clicks the <em>Unassigned</em> tile: the table filters. Clicks <em>2 - Major</em> in the severity chart: filters further.</li>
  <li>Exports the result as CSV for the stand-up.</li>
  <li>Presses <em>Mark all as seen</em>. Tomorrow, NEW and UPDATED markers show exactly what changed overnight.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Journey 3: a visitor trying the demo</h2>
<p>Opens the GitHub Pages site. With no server available, the page detects <em>demo mode</em> and generates sample data in the browser. Every feature works, including simulated JARVIS events, so the visitor can hear a briefing without connecting anything.</p>

<h2>Journey 4: the operator</h2>
<p>Deploys with Wrangler, sets secrets, registers the Atlassian app, watches logs with <code>wrangler tail</code>, checks CPU metrics, and lets the weekly personal-data report run. All of it is described in <a href="deploy-cloud.html">Deploy the Cloud edition</a> and <a href="operate.html">Operating in production</a>.</p>

<h2>What this tells the design</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Need from the journeys</th><th>Design consequence</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Notifications when the laptop is closed</td><td>Monitoring must run on a server on a schedule (cron), not in the page; delivery needs Web Push and a service worker</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Anyone can sign in, nothing to install</td><td>A hosted backend with OAuth, multi-user isolation, encrypted tokens</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Try before connecting</td><td>A demo mode that needs no server at all</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Never miss a reopen, never repeat</td><td>Change detection from the changelog with stable ids, not from timestamps</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Free to host</td><td>Fit inside Cloudflare's free limits: small, incremental work per minute</td></tr>
</table>
